            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hello. I'm working a bit on this, but I have a question. \n\nFor the following ssh config:\n\n```\nHost hello\n    HostName hello.example.com\n\nHost goodbye,bye\n    HostName goodbye.example.com\n\nHost nope,not.*,!yes,never\n    HostName idk.com\n    Port 1234\n```\n\nCurrent code in `parse_ssh_config` will return the following hostnames:\n\n```lua\n{ \"hello\", \"goodbye,bye\" }\n```\n\nBut, as mentioned in @eamonburns's comment, I think that a correct parser should return the following hostnames:\n\n```lua\n{ \"hello\", \"goodbye\", \"bye\", \"nope\", \"yes\", \"never\" }\n```\n\nAre we going to preserve the current behavior of the function, or change the result and modify the code that uses it accordingly? Also, #39378 adds a few features to this parser, so should I wait for that pull request to get merged before starting to work on this?",
